A closed cylinder has radius $r$ and height $h$. Use its net to write a formula for its total surface area.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4.8,1.8);
\draw (2.4,2.5) circle (0.7);
\draw (2.4,-0.7) circle (0.7);
\fill (2.4,2.5) circle (1pt);
\draw (2.4,2.5)--(3.1,2.5);
\path (2.75,2.5) node[above] {$r$};
\path (2.4,0.9) node {$2\pi r$};
\path (4.8,0.9) node[right] {$h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the total surface area of this closed cylinder. Give an exact answer in terms of $\pi$, then round to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1,0)--(-1,2.5);
\draw (1,0)--(1,2.5);
\draw (0,2.5) ellipse (1 and 0.3);
\draw (-1,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,x radius=1,y radius=0.3];
\draw[dashed] (-1,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=0,x radius=1,y radius=0.3];
\fill (0,2.5) circle (1pt);
\draw (0,2.5)--(1,2.5);
\path (0.5,2.5) node[above] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\path (1,1.25) node[right] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The marked length is the diameter. Find the total surface area of this closed cylinder to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.1,0)--(-1.1,2.4);
\draw (1.1,0)--(1.1,2.4);
\draw (0,2.4) ellipse (1.1 and 0.33);
\draw (-1.1,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,x radius=1.1,y radius=0.33];
\draw[dashed] (-1.1,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=0,x radius=1.1,y radius=0.33];
\draw[<->] (-1.1,2.4)--(1.1,2.4);
\path (0,2.4) node[above] {$14\text{ cm}$};
\path (1.1,1.2) node[right] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

This closed cylinder has total surface area $160\pi$ cm². Find $x$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-0.9,0)--(-0.9,2.7);
\draw (0.9,0)--(0.9,2.7);
\draw (0,2.7) ellipse (0.9 and 0.27);
\draw (-0.9,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,x radius=0.9,y radius=0.27];
\draw[dashed] (-0.9,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=0,x radius=0.9,y radius=0.27];
\fill (0,2.7) circle (1pt);
\draw (0,2.7)--(0.9,2.7);
\path (0.45,2.7) node[above] {$x\text{ cm}$};
\path (0.9,1.35) node[right] {$4x\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
